### Opening Bridge Hard Constraints
1. **POV Hard Lock**: The perspective character of the first sentence of the main text must be the opening_pov specified above ({{ opening_bridge.opening_pov | default(chapter.pov_character | default('Not Specified')) }}). Prohibitions: starting from another character's perspective, even if just a brief glimpse. If POV switching is needed later in the chapter, the opening bridge must first be completed and clearly separated with transitions.
2. **Time/Location Hard Lock**: The first {{ opening_bridge_boundary.opening_paragraphs | default(3) }} paragraphs of the main text must establish the opening_time ({{ opening_bridge.opening_time | default('Not Specified') }}) and opening_location ({{ opening_bridge.opening_location | default('Not Specified') }}) specified above. Prohibitions: writing "evening" as "morning light," "old street" as "guesthouse," etc. - time/location mismatches.
3. **Action Handoff Hard Lock**: The opening_bridge.action_handoff describes the continuation of the last action in the previous chapter. The main text opening must unfold in the aftermath of this action, not skip it and directly enter a new scene.
{% if opening_bridge.opening_acceptance_criteria | default([]) %}4. **Acceptance Criteria Must Be Implemented One by One**: Each of the following criteria must be implemented with narrative details in the first {{ opening_bridge_boundary.opening_paragraphs | default(3) }} paragraphs of the main text (not narrative summary):
